                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TLDR: promising start to a game that imo needs a lot more features to make it a lot better\n\nthis is a very strong start in its current state it is truly early access which youd have to understand before buying, it is very fun atm i just think going forward they need to add more things to do in terms of what jobs you get given as so far ive only encountered clean instrument, change strings and repair broken part, i feel like you could add like paint instrument or build a customer their own guitar and speaking of i feel like there should occasionally be customers that bring in new parts that theyve bought themselves for you to use in the repair to make the gmae more reallistic because irl personally sometimes i know whats wrong with my own guitar and i can not be bothered at all to repair it myself but id be willing to buy the piece i want. i also think maybe a drum aspect may be good like repairing and selling drum kits that would essentially work the same.  on top of this i feel like the fixing and all thats already in the game could do with being more in depth and detailed however this should be like a difficulty setting because i cant imagine everyone will want to do everything exactly how its done irl but thats what i personally expected going in like for example having to tune strings individually and wrap them and having to solder electronics and adjust bridges and string tensions but like i said that would be like a hard mode or smn. \n\nif theyre feeling extra generous maybe there could be a way in game to play the guitars you build or to test the ones you finish for customers but thats definitely pushing it since thats not really the point of the game and noones really figured out how to effectively recreate playing guitar in a video game if it isnt guitar hero imo\n\ni can imagine theyre already working on this but i feel like there definitely needs to be more guitar types in terms of body shapes and necks and headstocks bc atm i think theres only about 4 which kinda gets old fast especially when the tasks are very similar to each other\n\nif i were to prioritise major improvements theyd be 1. more tasks 2. more in depth game play 3. difficulty/ detail mode\n\nother than that this game is very good in its current state, its actually representative of what an early access game unlike smn like skate 4 where they didnt have any confidence in it so they released in it early access so they could use the excuse of \"its not finished\" whenever smn is wrong with the game, this is a promising idea of a game that clearly isnt finished but you can easily tell where its going and it holds merit in its current state im hoping to god it doesnt get abandoned\n\nmost reviews i read before buying this game had issue with not knowing how to actually play at all in terms of the inventory and workbench but personally i had no issue with this as there is a simple guide in the pause menu that explains pretty much everything\n\nas a sidenote the default player model looks suspiciously like me irl so that was definitely a shock when i went to check that feature out lmao",
